{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/643809-understudy-to-the-apex-apprentice-fearmaking","id":643809,"title":"Understudy to the Apex: Apprentice Fearmaking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-28T23:12:05-07:00","id":643809,"title":"Understudy to the Apex: Apprentice Fearmaking","content":"Ponderings on Kinship and staying Gorged (in combination with rereading the writeups for the Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches and the Lost Pantheon) got me to thinking about city dynamics in which the Apex is not a Beast but has Begotten hangers-on of various stripes. Figured it was a sufficiently broad topic to warrant a thread for characters and story seeds and other workshopping.<br /> <br /> For instance, let's say the local Apex is the chief archivist of an unusually concentrated chapter of the Lord Sages, with a brood of &quot;library imps&quot; who're engaged in something of a symbiotic relationship with the entitlement's stock of lore and contacts to the point where their respective corners of the Lair effectively serve as specialty departments. What might be a good refinement on that Apex's basic concept? Going from there, what might the constituents of this brood be like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-29-2015, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T00:55:47-07:00","id":643863,"title":"","content":"Well first of all, you'd have to decide what court this sage is, since that will certainly color their impression on the local primordial dream.<br /> <br /> A court like autumn, which cultivates fear, for example, is a natural fit, whereas a court like winter, well it would be a very incompetent winter courtier who somehow becomes the figure that looms largest in the local zeitgeist. <br /> <br /> And since courts are do it yourself in second edition, that's an even harder question to answer than normal. <br /> <br /> A lord sage of the autumn court would leave an impression of urban legends, a lord sage of the court of Scheherazade would make the primordial dream more about faerie tales and narrative tropes.<br /> <br /> Seeming would also factor in, a darkling would probably leave a different imprint than a fairest or a wizened.<br /> <br /> I can't help but figure that to know the beasts that would thrive under and cooperate with a specific Apex, you have to understand the specific Apex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T04:26:54-07:00","id":643928,"title":"","content":"Fairly sure that the Lord Sages are strictly Autumn. I would assume that a port of anything related to the Seasonal Courts will keep those same courts in 2e.<br /> <br /> So, how do we refine the concept? By actually writing out the Apex herself. If the ling in question is the Apex, I imagine that the character would have to have the Crown as well; while I suppose you could argue the crown isn't necessary, titles = asskicking in Changeling, so I find it hard to wrap my head around. Remember that Autumn, while they do collect lore, are also HUGE into gathering secrets as well, so that's probably a huge component as well. The Ugallu Family, the Atavisms Mimir's Wisdom and Eye of Heaven would likely be favored here, plus I'd allow the We Know All Your Secrets Nightmare to learn through Kinship with the Autumn fae. <br /> <br /> But for the rest? Write up your Sage and go from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T22:30:36-07:00","id":644942,"title":"","content":"No, the requirements for the lord sages are wyrd 2, occult 3, and at least 2 occult specialties.<br /> <br /> So while autumn court is a natural fit for the occult scholars of the organization, since they are the seasonal court most interested in other supernaturals, any changeling can join the lord sages. <br /> <br /> And since the other half of the lord sages are diplomats, well if one looks for a diplomatic changeling I know autumn wouldn't be my first choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T22:32:04-07:00","id":644945,"title":"","content":"The Lord Sages are not strictly Autumn. The Entitlements that are strictly Autumn are the Ancient and Accepted Order of Bridgesmasons, the Magi of the Gilded Thorn, and the Scarecrow Ministry.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T03:16:07-07:00","id":647811,"title":"","content":"I believe there are a few more important questions that must be answered first before a proper picture of this Apex and it's Brood can take shape.<br /> <br /> For starters a Changeling Apex would most likely be an individual with a high Wyrd rating by the very nature of that force of storytale-like fate. Since the Begotten are also creaters of narrative and metaphore I would speculate that the &quot;Book Imps&quot; chose to be a Brood with this Apex because it has profound cunning and wisdom when it comes to subverting their own narrative to their favor (I.E. Out foxing the Huntsmen and their servants.)<br /> <br /> Secondly the nature of the Lord Sages of the Unknown Reaches is to delve into the mythology and magic of the other supernatural creatures of the World of Darkness in a hope to create new Contracts and find strong allies to use against the Gentry. Since this maner of work is often very specialized around a single other supernatural creature it makes the most sense to me to make the Apex a scholar of the Children and probably recruited the Book Imps to be retainer like individuals in exchange for it's own unique powers and lore. Regarless of the Court, which would influence their Legend and how the Apex both secures Glamour and handicap the Huntsmen, I imagine the Brood would make the most out of the two splats strenghts and specialize in Oneiromancy, Pledges, and Dimension Hopping (Got to love the Beast's Skeleton Key Power.)<br /> <br /> I'd show case how the Apex protects the Beasts from Heroes by detecting them early and tricking them into Pledges they have no hope of surviving or sicking them on it's Begotten Kin's enemies. While the Children help patrol the worlds and dreams for signs of the True Fae and the Huntsmen so that the Apex will always know then the Gentry ride on their territory. Beyond that the rest is best served to highlight the themes of the Chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T21:01:01-07:00","id":648566,"title":"","content":"Worth pointing out that the focus for the thread here is on non-Beast Apexes as fixtures <i>in Beast games</i> first and foremost. That being said, some particulars that spring to mind for further refinement of this first concept:<br /> <br /> 1. This is essentially an excuse to build heavily around a brood Lair with an extensive set of Advanced Libraries.<br /> 2. Said focal library serves as a justification for a lot of Beasts coming and going in pursuit of far-flung family (and Lord Sages doing likewise in pursuit of leads).<br /> 3. The extent of family resemblance both capitalized and otherwise serves to do something similar to goetia \u2014 the members of the brood emphasize different aspects of the Apex in their development.<br /> <br /> A sizable portion of the splat focuses are going to come down to aesthetics, for which a few other things may bear thought:<br /> 1. At least a portion of the Lair likely dips into some number of Hollows as lore-caches.<br /> 2. At least one significant Chamber probably ought to be the product of the Apex's activities.<br /> 3. The prospect of the Apex having gained their position through a resounding moment of awful revelation a la some routes to the Incarnate Inheritance and/or some manner of curse may serve to reconcile their relative reclusiveness if oneiromancy is insufficient.<br /> <br /> Some other considerations: High Mantle and a Personal Approach tied to the brood may help matters on the Changeling side of the equation, and determining whether the way the brood relates to the library has notable divisions likewise helps narrow Hungers and Families \u2014 Tyrants, Collectors, and Nemeses seem like the most suited to staffing and outfitting a massive magical lorehouse.<br /> <br /> There's also the matter of how straightforward the Apex's relation to their role ought to be \u2014 Antiquarian is the obvious choice of kith for a head librarian, but the new iteration of the Fireheart has metaphorical breadth that could ostensibly be used to justify a Ravager in the brood, and kiths like Lurker, Oracle, or Sandharrowed all add their own considerations to the Family spread and power focuses, along with providing little nudges to the overall aesthetics.<br /> <br /> Still mulling over whether to not just stick with the Great Courts, seeing as the alternative is essentially &quot;create a goodly chunk of an entire setting around which this Apex's hive exists as a basis for a Court system.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:36:13-07:00","id":652970,"title":"","content":"This also depends on weather the Changelings your dealing with are 1e or 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T00:11:20-07:00","id":654837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/643809-understudy-to-the-apex-apprentice-fearmaking?p=652970#post652970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also depends on weather the Changelings your dealing with are 1e or 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit, but at present the biggest issue with using 2e is that how Icons and the Hedge work isn't available knowledge.<br /> <br /> The more solidified tentatives and placeholders now stand at;<br /> \u2022 Haborym is an Ogre Fireheart whose escape from the Leaden Scroll Foundry culminated in a massive fire at the local library.<br /> \u2022 Censer (a Ravager Leviathan whose Horror rests in a Chamber made from the scene of that same fire) is one of the oldest members of the brood and often accompanies Haborym in his oneiromantic Glamour-gathering excursions.<br /> \u2022 Hecate (a Collector Giant whose Horror tends to occupy Chambers made from the dream-fallout of Haborym's less careful attentions) is another anchoring member of the brood and her hoard may contain a Prop as an example of really weird Kinships.<br /> <br /> Less definitely\u2026<br /> \u2022 Contemplating the prospect of embrace the crossover by building a Court system in a fashion that peripherally maps well to the Hungers, whereby Haborym is then a member of the Court that best resonates with either Ruin or Hoard.<br /> \u2022 Not sure whether to keep the Family makeup of the brood eclectic or essentially narrow the focus to three Families.<br /> \u2022 Likewise unsure how big to have the changeling and Beast populations of this city beyond the generalities of &quot;something appropriate for a busy metropolitan area with lots of people coming and going.&quot; Figure an unusually concentrated chapter of the Lord Sages has a local headcount of at least in the low teens and multiply that by five or six to get the approximate changeling population? Assume the heightened degree of crossover pursuit means at least two dozen Beasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}